
# English Version

# Honours & Recognition

## Acknowledgement of His Selflessness

The decision to donate his organs was an act of immense generosity and selflessness by **Mr. Kanagala Balarama Krishna** and his family.

In recognition of this noble act, **Jeevandan AP** awarded an **official Certificate of Appreciation** acknowledging his selfless contribution through organ donation.

This certificate stands as a formal recognition of an act that transformed a moment of profound loss into an opportunity to give life to others.

### Recognized by Jeevandan AP

Jeevandan AP has also recognized **Mr. K. Balaramakrishna** by including his **name and photograph in its official donor list**, under its *Life Savers — Our Donors* section.

The official Jeevandan Andhra Pradesh portal maintains a dedicated list recognizing organ donors. ([Jeevandaan][1])

[View the Jeevandan AP Donors List](https://jeevandan.ap.gov.in/nl/Donors.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

---

## Recognition for His Gift of Sight

His contribution did not stop with organ donation.

His **two eyes were also donated**, giving two other individuals the opportunity to regain vision.

In recognition of this gift of sight, **L V Prasad Eye Institute (LVPEI)** presented a **Certificate of Appreciation** acknowledging his eye donation.

LVPEI is a comprehensive eye-care institution with an established **Eye Banking** program and a dedicated eye-donation service. ([LVPEI][2])

[L V Prasad Eye Institute — Official Website](https://www.lvpei.org/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

---

## A Legacy Officially Remembered

These certificates are more than pieces of paper.

They are **official acknowledgements of a selfless decision**—a decision that allowed something meaningful to continue even after his life had ended.

His name being remembered among the donors of Jeevandan AP, together with the recognition received for his eye donation, stands as a lasting record of the generosity that defined his final act.

**His life touched people around him.
His final act reached beyond them.
And his name now remains recorded among those who gave others the gift of life and sight.**

